lisa-design:
- release.yml keeps its file name but now runs on release: published (release-ui.yml, v1.4.0); docker.yml (only called by the old release.yml) is deleted. images input names "ui" explicitly, as mock-ui does, so the GHCR name stays ghcr.io/compliance-framework/ui.
- Artifact shape: same image name, linux/amd64+linux/arm64 (plus the two attestation manifests both old and new indexes carry), same version tags X.Y.Z/X.Y/X/latest and X.Y.Z-rcN. The release no longer pushes sha-<7>; preview's on-main run publishes sha-<7> for the same commit (release-please and cut-prerelease both tag main's head). Old metadata-action labels (title, description, licenses, version, created, url) are not reproduced: publish-image.yml sets only source and revision and has no labels input.
- "Keep the build cache": not reproducible and not needed. publish-image.yml has no cache input, and the old cross-run cache never worked (actions/cache got an empty key; the v2.12.1 run logged "Input required and not supplied: key"). The old local buildx cache only reused the build stage inside one job; the new flow builds each arch once, natively (no QEMU).
- preview: kind image, on-main true, concurrency group preview-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }} (mock baseline). cut-prerelease caller per plan.
